  "storage": "Pickled carrot and daikon keep 2 weeks in the fridge and are better on day three than day one. Grilled pork keeps 3 days. ⚠️ Cooked broken rice goes hard in the fridge faster than whole grain does, because there is more exposed starch to retrograde — eat it the same day where you can, and steam rather than microwave what is left.",
  "chefNotes": "⚖️ The rice is the dish, so if you can only get one thing right, get that. A plate of excellent grilled pork over ordinary long-grain rice is a nice supper and it is not cơm tấm.\n\n✅ The chop wants to be thin. A centimetre and a half at most, butterflied or beaten flat if yours is thicker, because the marinade only ever reaches a few millimetres in and a thick chop is mostly unseasoned in the middle.\n\n⚠️ Fish sauce brands vary enormously in salt. Taste the marinade before the pork goes in — it should be aggressively savoury and slightly too sweet, because the fire will take the edge off both.\n\n⛔ Never rinse the pickle after squeezing. The salt draw is doing seasoning work, not just water removal, and washing it leaves the vegetables limp and bland at once.",
