  "storage": "Đồ chua keeps 2 weeks in the fridge and improves for the first three days. Pâté keeps 4 days covered with a film of butter on top. ⛔ An assembled bánh mì does not keep at all — the crust goes soft within the hour and there is no reviving it. Build to order.",
  "chefNotes": "⚖️ Buy the wrong bread and nothing else you do matters. Soft crust, light crumb, small loaf. If the only thing available is dense, hollow it out.\n\n✅ Both spreads, both faces, right to the edges. This is structural as much as it is about taste.\n\n⚠️ Chicken livers go from perfect to grainy in about a minute. Pull them while the centre is still faintly pink; residual heat finishes them in the blender.\n\n⛔ Whole coriander sprigs, stalks and all — not chopped. The stalk is where most of the aroma sits and chopped coriander disappears into the filling instead of hitting you on the first bite.",
  "pairsWith": "Iced Vietnamese coffee · Gỏi Cuốn alongside · Chè Chuối after",
